{
  "name": "RC placement workflow",
  "description": "Guided 7-step workflow: targets \u2192 RC heights \u2192 migration & jacking \u2192 elastic distribution \u2192 bell-crank progression \u2192 dampers & corner entry \u2192 iterate.",
  "pages": [
    {
      "title": "Targets & baseline",
      "layout": [
        {
          "type": "notes",
          "cfg": {
            "title": "Step 1 \u2013 set the targets",
            "text": "Goal: place the roll centres so the load-transfer distribution matches the targets, with **more geometric LT for a quick, stable response at peak**, then use a **bell-crank progressive rate** to stiffen the elastic path at large roll, and check it over several a_y and corners.\n\n- Set the targets on the right: LLTD front band (start near static front weight + 2\u20135 %), roll gradient, overshoot, geometric share at t0+50 ms, limit a_y.\n- Put your real car, tire and hardpoint data in the sidebar (all defaults are placeholders).\n- Switch **Geometric LT model = ic_angles** (sidebar \u2192 Manoeuvre) so RC migration and jacking are included.\n- Press **Set baseline** (top bar) before changing anything."
          },
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "w": 5,
          "h": 7
        },
        {
          "type": "targets",
          "cfg": {},
          "x": 5,
          "y": 0,
          "w": 7,
          "h": 5
        },
        {
