    {
      "title": "Place roll centres",
      "layout": [
        {
          "type": "notes",
          "cfg": {
            "title": "Step 2 \u2013 roll-centre heights",
            "text": "The map shows the limit a_y (colour) and the LLTD (contour lines) over front \u00d7 rear RC height. In adaptive mode every point moves the inboard pivots at constant ball joints and swing-arm length.\n\n- Look for the region where the LLTD contour sits inside your band **and** limit a_y is high.\n- Prefer higher RCs for more geometric (instant) LT, but watch jacking in step 3.\n- Drag the pinned RC sliders to the chosen point; the front views show the new geometry."
          },
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "w": 4,
          "h": 6
        },
        {
