    {
      "title": "RC migration & jacking vs a_y",
      "layout": [
        {
          "type": "notes",
          "cfg": {
            "title": "Step 3 \u2013 migration and jacking",
            "text": "With the IC-angle model the geometric LT uses the instant centres **at the rolled pose** and the inner/outer tire force split.\n\n- Effective RC height vs a_y should stay close to the static value (small migration).\n- RC lateral migration per degree of roll: smaller is more predictable.\n- Jacking force / ride-height change: keep it small; a high RC lifts the body (OptimumG \u2018Rolling about\u2019).\n- Compare several front RC heights in each sweep (\u2699 \u2192 compare values)."
          },
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "w": 4,
          "h": 6
        },
        {
          "type": "sweep",
          "cfg": {
            "x_path": "maneuver.ay_g",
            "x0": 0.2,
            "x1": 1.6,
            "n": 8,
            "compare_path": "front.h_rc_mm",
            "compare_values": "20, 50, 90",
            "output": "f.h_rc_eff",
            "limit": false,
            "transient": false
          },
          "x": 4,
          "y": 0,
          "w": 4,
          "h": 6
        },
        {
          "type": "sweep",
