    {
      "title": "Bell-crank progression",
      "layout": [
        {
          "type": "notes",
          "cfg": {
            "title": "Step 5 \u2013 progressive rate from the rocker",
            "text": "The rocker geometry sets MR(z) and therefore the wheel rate k_s\u00b7MR\u00b2 + F_s\u00b7dMR/dz. A **rising** MR stiffens the elastic path at large roll: less final roll and less overshoot, without stiffening small inputs.\n\n- Edit the rocker points (sidebar \u2192 Front/Rear bell-crank) or pin them here.\n- Watch MR and wheel rate vs travel, roll stiffness vs roll angle.\n- The transient roll angle shows the effect on overshoot at corner entry."
          },
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "w": 4,
          "h": 6
        },
